-- title:
--   Residual streams: events of $\sigma(\eta_0,\nu_k:k\notin S)$
-- statement:
--   For a set of buyers $S$, a stream $A\subseteq\Omega$ is **residual for $S$** if it is an event of the σ-algebra
--
--   $$
--   \sigma\bigl(\eta_0,\ \nu_k : k\notin S\bigr)
--   $$
--
--   generated by the common value component and the private signals of the buyers outside $S$.
--
--   The whole stream $\Omega$ is residual for every $S$. When the algorithm, at a stream $A$ residual for $S$, serves buyer $i\in S_1$ and recurses on $A\cap\{v_i<\theta_i\}$ with buyers $S_1\setminus\{i\}$, the new stream is residual for the new buyer set. On a residual stream the signals of the buyers in $S$ are independent of the stream, which is what the paper's Lemma 7 and eq. (10) use.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper states Lemma 7 for "an arbitrary set of impressions"; it is false for an arbitrary measurable set (counterexample in the Lemma 7 milestone) and true on residual streams, which are the streams the algorithm visits.
-- source:
--   Kim, Mirrokni & Nazerzadeh, Deals or No Deals: Contract Design for Online Advertising, SSRN 2693037, Proof of Lemma 5, p.28 ("$\mathcal I$ is conditioned on some events involving the common value component $\eta_0$ and the private valuations $\nu_j$ of the buyers offered deals already")

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PrefDeals_ValuationModel

open MeasureTheory

namespace PrefDeals

/-- The σ-algebra `σ(η₀, νₖ : k ∉ S)` generated by the common value and the signals of the buyers
outside `S`. -/
abbrev residualSigma {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {P : Measure Ω} {n : ℕ}
    (M : ValuationModel P n) (S : Finset (Fin n)) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  MeasurableSpace.comap M.eta0 inferInstance ⊔
    ⨆ (k : Fin n) (_ : k ∉ S), MeasurableSpace.comap (M.nu k) inferInstance

/-- **Residual streams for a set of buyers.**
Kim, Mirrokni & Nazerzadeh, *Deals or No Deals*, SSRN 2693037, Proof of Lemma 5, p.28: "Note that
`𝓘` is conditioned on some events involving the common value component `η₀` and the private
valuations `νⱼ` of the buyers offered deals already in the previous iterations (i.e., `j ∉ S`). In
particular, the private signals `νⱼ` for the buyers in `S` are independent and unconditioned."

`IsResidual M S A` says that the stream `A ⊆ Ω` is an event of `σ(η₀, νₖ : k ∉ S)`. The whole stream
`Ω` is residual for every `S`, and every stream the algorithm reaches with buyer set `S` is residual
for `S`.

**Formalization Note.** This is the class of impression sets on which the paper uses Lemma 7 and
(10) (p.28). Lemma 7 fails on an arbitrary measurable set of impressions. -/
def IsResidual {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {P : Measure Ω} {n : ℕ}
    (M : ValuationModel P n) (S : Finset (Fin n)) (A : Set Ω) : Prop :=
  MeasurableSet[residualSigma M S] A

end PrefDeals


